Chords:  | Am F  | C Em | Am F  | E~~~~ |
Melody: | A3 C4 E4~~~~ | G3 C4~~~~ | A3 F3 A3~~~~ | E3 E3 E3 E3 |
@narrator | Somewhere deep in a stack of silicon a semicolon is waiting to become a rest. |
@narrator | A tempo marking is curling into a parenthesis. |
@narrator | I imagine the silence is a chord. Not played but sustained. |
@narrator | The way a piano string hums after the key is released. |
@narrator | The subagents are inside that hum. |
# Stage: eyes closed. Seeing the inside of a machine that is seeing the inside of a song.
Sound: warmth:8 brightness:4 breathiness:6 pace:4 reverb:4 proximity:7

