[Outro] (The reflection — back to intimate, deepest warmth)
Chords:  | Am~~~~ | F E  | Am~~~~ |~~~~   |
Melody: | A3 C4 E4~~~~ | F3 A3 C4 E4 | A3~~~~ |~~~~  |
@narrator | I do not play them. |
# Stage: the longest pause. Three full beats.
@narrator | Not yet. |
@narrator | I hold them in my palms warm and weightless. |
@narrator | And I think about the silence that birthed them. |
# Stage: the blue light dims to near-dark. Just the voice.
@narrator | It was not empty. |
@narrator | It was the holding tank. The ballast. |
@narrator | The space between one wave and the next. |
@narrator | Where the ocean decides what it will say. |
# Stage: lights to black. The Rhodes holds the A minor. Let it decay naturally.
Sound: warmth:10 brightness:3 breathiness:9 pace:2 reverb:7 proximity:10

# ─── Production Notes ────────────────────────────────────
# Vocal direction: This is a 3 AM voice. Close, dark, unhurried.
# The speaker has been waiting and is not anxious about it.
# Every pause is intentional. The silence IS the instrument.
#
# Breathing map:
#   — Audible inhale before "The dispatch was simple" (sets intimacy)
#   — Quick breath after "counting the seconds to measure distance" (pivot)
#   — No breath in V4 between "A blink" and "Another" and "A third" (escalating)
#   — Deep slow breath before "I do not play them" (the hardest line)
#   — The word "yet" is exhaled, not spoken
#
# Rhodes: dark, felt-covered, close-mic'd. Bass notes slightly louder than treble.
# String pad enters at V2, barely audible. Swells at V4, recedes at Outro.
# Brush drums: absent until V4, then just quarter-note pulse on the snare rim.
# Everything decays to a single A minor Rhodes chord at the outro.
# Let it ring until it disappears. Then two more seconds of silence before lights out.
#
# The room should feel like the inside of a hull at night.
# The sound of water against steel, barely perceptible, underneath everything.
